From: CoolFreeze23 <34906576+CoolFreeze23@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: correct the REO hold warning size

The comment on ATH12K_DP_RX_REO_DESC_HOLD_WARN (patch 349) says 256 held
descriptors are about 8 MB. Each QoS queue descriptor is a 2 KB
allocation (sized for a 1024 BA window: 1663 bytes), so 256 are about
512 KB, the queues of about 15 peers. Comment only.
---
diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/dp_rx.h b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/dp_rx.h
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/dp_rx.h
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/dp_rx.h
@@ -72,7 +72,8 @@ struct ath12k_dp_rx_reo_cmd {
 #define ATH12K_DP_RX_REO_DESC_FREE_THRES  64
 #define ATH12K_DP_RX_REO_DESC_FREE_TIMEOUT_MS 1000
 /* warn (once a minute) when more REO queue descriptors than this are held
- * for peers whose delete firmware has not confirmed (about 8 MB)
+ * for peers whose delete firmware has not confirmed: each QoS descriptor is
+ * a 2 KB allocation, so about 512 KB, the queues of about 15 peers
  */
 #define ATH12K_DP_RX_REO_DESC_HOLD_WARN 256
 
